import json
CONTRACT = json.loads("{\"semantic_version\":\"1.0.0\",\"server_name\":\"signalbase-monitoring-v3\",\"instructions\":\"Monitoring watches a chosen set of companies and delivers their signals as they happen; the search tools answer questions about the whole database. Use these tools when someone names accounts to follow, not to look things up. Read list_monitors before creating anything, and reuse a fitting monitor instead of making a near-duplicate. One monitor carries one signal selection for every target it holds, so different selections mean different monitors. These tools change a customer's account. Confirm the monitor and the list with the user before the first write of a conversation, add targets with dry_run:true whenever the list did not come from the user verbatim, and report what actually happened — added, skipped as already present, rejected as unparseable — rather than assuming the whole input landed. Targets resolve asynchronously. A pending target is matched by automatic research within minutes to hours and re-checked nightly; it delivers nothing until it resolves, and it needs no action from you. Never tell a user a pending target has failed or ask them to re-add it. Monitoring is forward-looking: adding a company does not replay signals it already has. Use the signal search tools for history. Stopping is update_monitor with active:false, which keeps every target and can be undone. There is no delete tool; if someone asks to delete a monitor, say it is done from the Monitoring page. Company-level signals are what a monitor delivers. It does not return a company's decision-makers or contacts; people are searched separately. Monitors created here deliver by email to the API key's owner. Webhook delivery exists but is deliberately not exposed to connectors: attaching an endpoint returns a signing secret exactly once, and a secret must not pass through a model's context or a chat transcript. Direct anyone who wants webhook delivery to the Monitoring page or the REST API; never claim you can add, read or rotate a webhook here.\",\"tools\":[{\"name\":\"create_monitor\",\"description\":\"Create a monitor: a named group of watched companies with its own signal selection. Start here when someone wants to follow specific accounts rather than search. Returns the monitor id used by every other tool. The monitor starts empty — follow with add_monitor_targets. A team may hold at most 20 monitors. Free. Monitors created here deliver by email to the API key's owner. Webhook delivery exists but is deliberately not exposed to connectors: attaching an endpoint returns a signing secret exactly once, and a secret must not pass through a model's context or a chat transcript. Direct anyone who wants webhook delivery to the Monitoring page or the REST API; never claim you can add, read or rotate a webhook here.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255,\"description\":\"What this monitor watches, in the user's words — for example \\\"Key accounts\\\" or \\\"Series A prospects\\\".\"},\"signal_types\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"funding_round\",\"acquisition\",\"job_change\",\"hiring\"]},\"minItems\":1,\"maxItems\":4,\"description\":\"Signal types this monitor delivers. funding_round: the company raises a round. acquisition: it acquires or is acquired. job_change: someone joins or leaves. hiring: it posts a new job. Applies to every target in the monitor — use separate monitors for different selections.\"}},\"required\":[\"name\",\"signal_types\"],\"additionalProperties\":false,\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":false,\"openWorldHint\":true}},{\"name\":\"list_monitors\",\"description\":\"List every monitor on the team with its signal selection, paused state and statistics: how many targets it holds, how many are matched to a company, signals in the last 30 days, and when it last delivered. Read this before creating a monitor so an existing one is reused rather than duplicated. Free.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{},\"additionalProperties\":false,\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":false,\"openWorldHint\":true}},{\"name\":\"get_monitor\",\"description\":\"Read one monitor with the same fields list_monitors returns. Use after a change to confirm the current state. Free.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"monitor_id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255,\"description\":\"Monitor id returned by create_monitor or list_monitors.\"}},\"required\":[\"monitor_id\"],\"additionalProperties\":false,\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":false,\"openWorldHint\":true}},{\"name\":\"update_monitor\",\"description\":\"Change a monitor's name, its signal selection, or whether it is active. signal_types replaces the whole list rather than adding to it, so include every type that should remain. active:false pauses delivery and keeps every target, and active:true resumes it — this is the way to stop a monitor, and the only reversible one. Free.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"monitor_id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255,\"description\":\"Monitor id returned by create_monitor or list_monitors.\"},\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255},\"signal_types\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"funding_round\",\"acquisition\",\"job_change\",\"hiring\"]},\"minItems\":1,\"maxItems\":4,\"description\":\"Signal types this monitor delivers. funding_round: the company raises a round. acquisition: it acquires or is acquired. job_change: someone joins or leaves. hiring: it posts a new job. Applies to every target in the monitor — use separate monitors for different selections.\"},\"active\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"false pauses delivery and keeps every target; true resumes it. This is how monitoring is stopped — there is no delete tool.\"}},\"required\":[\"monitor_id\"],\"additionalProperties\":false,\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":false,\"openWorldHint\":true}},{\"name\":\"add_monitor_targets\",\"description\":\"Add companies to a monitor, by website domain, LinkedIn company URL or LinkedIn member profile URL, up to 100 per call. Adding is idempotent: targets already in the monitor are reported as skipped rather than duplicated, and unparseable entries are reported without failing the call. Targets matched to a known company resolve immediately and start delivering; the rest are pending and researched automatically. A team may watch 1000 targets in total, and a call that would exceed that is rejected whole, adding nothing. Use dry_run:true first for any list the user has not seen you repeat back. Free.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"monitor_id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255,\"description\":\"Monitor id returned by create_monitor or list_monitors.\"},\"targets\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":500},\"minItems\":1,\"maxItems\":100,\"description\":\"Company website domains, LinkedIn company URLs, or LinkedIn member profile URLs, in any mix. A profile URL monitors whichever company that person currently works at. Scheme, www., path and case are normalized away, so repeats of a target already in the monitor are skipped rather than duplicated. At most 100 per call.\"},\"dry_run\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"true reports what this exact call would add, skip as already present, and reject as unparseable, plus the team's remaining capacity — and writes nothing. Use it to confirm a long list with the user before committing.\"}},\"required\":[\"monitor_id\",\"targets\"],\"additionalProperties\":false,\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true,\"openWorldHint\":true}},{\"name\":\"list_monitor_targets\",\"description\":\"List a monitor's targets with each one's resolution status, matched company and most recent signal. Filter by status to see what is still pending. Paginated, newest first; read total before assuming a page is the whole monitor. Free.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"monitor_id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255,\"description\":\"Monitor id returned by create_monitor or list_monitors.\"},\"status\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"resolved\",\"pending\"],\"description\":\"resolved: matched to a company, signals are flowing. pending: not matched yet, researched automatically and re-checked nightly, delivering nothing meanwhile. Omit for both.\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":1,\"maximum\":200},\"offset\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"minimum\":0,\"maximum\":100000}},\"required\":[\"monitor_id\"],\"additionalProperties\":false,\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":false,\"openWorldHint\":true}},{\"name\":\"remove_monitor_targets\",\"description\":\"Stop watching specific companies in one monitor, by the same identifiers add_monitor_targets accepts or by target id. Entries that match nothing are reported in not_found rather than failing the call. Removing every target leaves the monitor in place and delivering nothing; to stop a whole monitor use update_monitor with active:false instead. Free.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"monitor_id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255,\"description\":\"Monitor id returned by create_monitor or list_monitors.\"},\"targets\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":500},\"minItems\":1,\"maxItems\":100,\"description\":\"Company website domains, LinkedIn company URLs, or LinkedIn member profile URLs, in any mix. A profile URL monitors whichever company that person currently works at. Scheme, www., path and case are normalized away, so repeats of a target already in the monitor are skipped rather than duplicated. At most 100 per call.\"},\"target_ids\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":255},\"minItems\":1,\"maxItems\":100,\"description\":\"Target ids as returned by list_monitor_targets.\"}},\"required\":[\"monitor_id\"],\"additionalProperties\":false,\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"},\"annotations\":{\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true,\"openWorldHint\":true}}],\"concepts\":{\"target_kinds\":{\"domain\":\"A company website domain or any URL on it (acme.com, https://www.acme.com/about). Monitors that company.\",\"linkedin_company\":\"A LinkedIn company page URL. Monitors that company. Use when the user has the LinkedIn page but not the website.\",\"linkedin_profile\":\"A LinkedIn member profile URL. Monitors whichever company that person currently works at, so it follows them if they move.\"},\"target_status\":{\"resolved\":\"Matched to a company in the Signalbase database; its signals are delivered from now on.\",\"pending\":\"Not matched yet. Researched automatically and re-checked nightly. Delivers nothing meanwhile and needs no user action.\"},\"signal_types\":{\"funding_round\":\"The monitored company raised a round.\",\"acquisition\":\"The monitored company acquired, or was acquired.\",\"job_change\":\"Someone joined or left the monitored company.\",\"hiring\":\"The monitored company posted a new job.\"},\"limits\":{\"monitors_per_team\":20,\"targets_per_team\":1000,\"targets_per_call\":100,\"credits\":\"Every monitoring tool is free; no call consumes credits.\"},\"delivery\":\"A monitor delivers by email to the API key's owner while it is active and holds at least one resolved target. Monitors created here deliver by email to the API key's owner. Webhook delivery exists but is deliberately not exposed to connectors: attaching an endpoint returns a signing secret exactly once, and a secret must not pass through a model's context or a chat transcript. Direct anyone who wants webhook delivery to the Monitoring page or the REST API; never claim you can add, read or rotate a webhook here.\"},\"examples\":[{\"name\":\"create_monitor\",\"arguments\":{\"name\":\"Key accounts\",\"signal_types\":[\"funding_round\",\"hiring\"]}},{\"name\":\"add_monitor_targets\",\"arguments\":{\"monitor_id\":\"29681a72-ed3d-41a8-b119-2c2942b34996\",\"targets\":[\"acme.com\",\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/initech/\",\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jane-doe/\"],\"dry_run\":true}},{\"name\":\"list_monitor_targets\",\"arguments\":{\"monitor_id\":\"29681a72-ed3d-41a8-b119-2c2942b34996\",\"status\":\"pending\"}},{\"name\":\"update_monitor\",\"arguments\":{\"monitor_id\":\"29681a72-ed3d-41a8-b119-2c2942b34996\",\"active\":false}}],\"contract_hash\":\"161c6ca8844d0a8032d2e6c98d4a899e32b1421b92ccf1d967a6b2ae44c02c30\"}")
